         "cssStyle": "",
         "label": "module_7",
         "name": "module_7",
         "params": {
          "align": "left",
          "body_size": 17,
          "content": "<p><strong style='color: #012638'>GMP is the FDA's framework for supplement manufacturing.</strong> It covers every aspect of production: facility cleanliness, equipment calibration, batch record documentation, raw material verification, testing protocols, packaging integrity, and shipping conditions.</p><p>Being GMP <em>compliant</em> means we follow these practices. Being GMP <em>certified</em> by NSF and SQF means an independent third party audits our facility to verify we actually do. The difference matters: certification requires unannounced inspections, documentation review, and continuous evidence of compliance.</p><p>For private label brands, this means you can confidently tell your customers that every product you sell was manufactured under the same standards as the brands they already trust.</p>",
          "css_class": "dnd-module",
          "heading_size": 32,
          "max_width": 800,
          "module_id": 218940115784,
          "style": {
